# width: 120
# height: 40
# The info view (the help box at the bottom of the left column) reads
# the curated dictionary (`src/app/info_view_copy/`) before the
# tooltip's one-liner: a statusline segment, a launcher-dock item and a
# Settings row each show their entry's title, and a target with no
# entry shows the tooltip's line marked `no help written yet`. The
# coordinates are 120x40's: the statusline is row 38, an `always` dock
# with `.inner` placement is row 37 with the `+ New` item at the END of the
# run (84..91; `ui.dock.plus_at = right` since dock-polish — Browser /
# Claude Code / Codex / HTTP / New terminal sit to its left), and the
# Settings overlay's first row (`Line numbers`) sits where it sits.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
# The mode chip, leftmost on the statusline.
hover 1 38
expect screen contains "Mode chip — standard"
expect screen lacks "no help written yet"
# The launcher dock's `+` item.
ex dock always
expect screen contains "New terminal"
hover 87 37
expect screen contains "+ New…"
expect screen lacks "no help written yet"
# A Settings row: the overlay's first row, `Line numbers`.
command view.settings
expect screen contains "Line numbers"
hover 40 10
expect screen contains "The line-number"
expect screen lacks "no help written yet"
key esc
# A curated menu row: the Keymap chip's menu opens above the statusline
# (rows 33..38 at this size); its last row is `Open the cheatsheet`.
rightclick 1 38
expect screen contains "Open the cheatsheet"
hover 4 37
expect screen contains "The cheatsheet"
key esc
# Phase two: every context-menu row is curated — the position chip's
# `Copy position (1:1)` row, which carries the cursor's own text, is
# matched by its label's prefix and reads its entry, never the
# `Cursor: Copy position` fallback (hover_help_menus.test walks six
# more menus).
rightclick 72 38
expect screen contains "Copy position"
hover 76 37
expect screen contains "Copy the cursor"
expect screen contains "Copies the"
expect screen lacks "Cursor: Copy position"
expect screen lacks "no help written yet"
key esc
